  "reason": "With no prior experiments, there is no evidence to guide exploitation, so the priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest RNA configuration: PCA is a standard, fast linear encoder unlikely to be a bottleneck, and singleprofile avoids confounding from aggregation. This gives a well-defined reference accuracy for RNA alone, against which I can later compare (a) whether a learned encoder (scvi, scgpt) helps, (b) whether multiprofile + aggregation adds value, (c) whether image modality adds value, and (d) whether multimodal fusion outperforms either single modality. Choosing the simplest baseline first maximizes the interpretability of every subsequent comparison within the 10-experiment budget."
